- Every direct formula aliquot is at least 10 uL. The two desired 2 uL neat-equivalent motif doses are delivered through separately prepared 10% v/v DPG stocks.
- Physical smell, LNDL similarity, liking, hedonism, depth, richness, transition quality, safety, stability, diffusion, longevity, maturation, and release remain `NOT TESTED / HOLD`.

## Target identity and excluded takeovers

The protected subject is a cardamom-led La Nuit nocturne: a cold aromatic capsule opens through controlled lavender into warm coumarinic seed tissue, violet-suede tailoring, literal cedar/vetiver, yielding wood, and creamy intimate skin. Juniper and Blue Chamomile are two orthogonal modifiers of that one subject, not a new perfume chassis.

- **Juniper function:** cool dry berry/conifer definition around the cardamom capsule; never gin, pine cleaner, or generic aromatic-fougere takeover.
- **Blue Chamomile function:** a small sweet-herbaceous/tobacco/azulenic shadow braided into lavender, coumarin, immortelle, and violet cloth; never medicinal tea, bitter herb, muddy natural, rose-species floral, or tobacco object.
- **Hedonic hierarchy:** overall liking, opening pleasure, transition pleasure, drydown pleasure, and re-smell desire govern advancement after the LNDL identity floor is met. Modeling cannot promote an unpleasant arm.
- **Excluded:** aquatic-blue materials; rose; geranium; osmanthus; clove; caraway; cinnamon candy; pastry; apple; vanilla dessert; explicit tobacco; smoke; leather; lipstick iris; oud; incense; stacked musks; generic amberwood wall; prestige-natural accumulation.

