## Spatial and temporal transition map

| Window | Front | Living middle | Rear / residue | Required relationship |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0–5 min | Cardamom capsule, bitter rind, optional dry juniper edge | Terpinyl/linalyl shell and Bontoux lavender | Violet-metal and cedar glints | Juniper clarifies cardamom without becoming gin or pine cleaner |
| 5–30 min | Capsule contracts | Lavender exposes optional azulene shadow and Jessemal/coumarin tissue | Leaf-metal and root seams become legible | Chamomile must feel like the shadow of the hinge, not a new herbal tea accord |
| 30–120 min | Aromatic seed residue | Coumarin, Tonkarome, tonka grain, heliotropal, immortelle, violet-suede cloth | Cedar/vetiver and Ebanol form around the interior | Blue shadow may deepen nocturnality but must not create medicinal, muddy, bitter, or tobacco takeover |
| 2–6 h | Violet-root tailoring | Yielding wood and coumarinic skin | Cedar/vetiver verticality under bounded pressure | Tenderness and dry contour coexist without an amberwood wall |
| 6–24 h | Faint aromatic edge | Hayed almond and creamy skin echo | Pencil cedar and root residue | Late residue recalls the cardamom-lavender subject without false top persistence |

All temporal statements are design intent, not observed evolution.

